User: Design and create an AI agent that manages team tasks with functionalities: create tasks, schedule tasks, close tasks, add notes to tasks, list tasks, and search tasks. Include planning for database schema if needed and write the prompt based on standard agent template. +
Assistant: I've analyzed the existing database and found no 'Tasks' table. To support the task management agent, I need to create two new tables:

1. **Tasks** - to store task details
2. **TaskNotes** - to store notes associated with tasks, with user attribution and timestamps

Here is the exact SQL I propose to execute:

```sql
-- Create Tasks table
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS Tasks (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    title TEXT NOT NULL,
    description TEXT,
    assignee_id INTEGER,
    created_by INTEGER NOT NULL,
    project_id INTEGER,
    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'open',
    priority TEXT DEFAULT 'medium',
    due_date DATETIME,
    scheduled_date DATETIME,
    completion_date DATETIME,
    created_at DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    updated_at DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    FOREIGN KEY (assignee_id) REFERENCES Users(id),
    FOREIGN KEY (created_by) REFERENCES Users(id),
    FOREIGN KEY (project_id) REFERENCES Projects(id)
);

-- Create TaskNotes table
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS TaskNotes (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    task_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
    user_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
    note_text TEXT NOT NULL,
    created_at DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    FOREIGN KEY (task_id) REFERENCES Tasks(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES Users(id)
);
```

